//    so the model is quickly forced into a constrained span.
// 3. The managed span helper handles all span state, parser validity, and closing
//    with AdaptiveConstrainedStep internally.
// 4. This is the simplest possible correct approach - delegate everything to the
//    high-level managed helper that has proven correctness.
//
// The key insight: GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan handles the entire loop
// including free preamble, forced span entry, constrained generation, and span
// closure. With prefixBudget=10, the model gets at most 10 free tokens before
// being forced into the constrained span.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
//   GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan's postcondition guarantees
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
